    <h2>Town Events</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Night of the Whispers</strong> – March 15: Reenactment of Eleanor’s first vision.</li>
      <li><strong>Train Whistle Poetry Night</strong> – March 11, Midnight: A lucky townsperson reads a poetry over the noise of the midnight train, the Crescent.</li>
      <li><strong>Eleanor’s Gala</strong> – April 1: Eleanor's 75th birthday is no joke! Community potluck.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Town Lore</h2>
    <div class="quote">
      “If you hear the crows before the church bells, turn around.” – Unknown
    </div>
    <p>Crows have always been part of Grace Hollow, but it was Miss Eleanor Grace who first claimed to understand them. Since the 1950s, she’s made predictions that few can explain, and most choose not to question.</p>

